{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Repeal and replace the 2026 ban on depictions of suffocation in pornography",
        "additional_details": "From 6 November, realistic pornographic depictions of suffocation or strangulation will be criminalised. The Act does not name certain sexual positions, yet some websites plan to remove fetish categories from UK access relating to those positions, because of the acts that they contain. Classified films have a statutory exemption from this legislation, whereas other creators face legal uncertainty, lost sales and removal of existing purchases. We believe the law needs proportionate boundaries that protect people without indiscriminately restricting consensual adult work.",
        "background": "We ask Parliament to repeal section 104 of the Crime and Policing Act 2026 and replace it with a narrower offence that distinguishes consensual, staged adult fetish performances from actual harm. Reverse its commencement, pending a review, and consult affected creators and platforms.",
